{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall not wrong one another, and you shall fear your Elohim.</b> This is verbal wronging (אונאת דברים) — that one should not vex his fellow nor give him counsel that is not fitting for him. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said: all the gates were locked except the gates of wrongdoing (אונאה), as it is said (Amos 7:7): ״הנה ה' נצב על חומת אנך ובידו אנך״. And the reason is that the wronged person suffers greatly and his mind is weakened, and his heart is broken over his affliction, and he prays out of the anxiety of his heart with proper intention (כוונה) and is heard. And if he says, 'And who knows whether I intended harm?' — therefore it is said, ויראת מאלהיך — 'and you shall fear your Elohim.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:15.877585781Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}